From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 16:41:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: give the touchscreen its reset line

GPIO 54 is already muxed and driven high for the touchscreen, but nothing
owns it, so the controller can never be restarted. Its avdd rail is shared
with the WCN3990 Wi-Fi chip and stays up whenever Wi-Fi is in use, which
leaves the driver unable to power-cycle the part and makes system resume
fail with -ENODEV.

Describe the line so the driver can pulse it. The stock device tree names
the same pin, GPIO 54, as the touchscreen reset, alongside GPIO 122 as its
interrupt, which matches the interrupt already described here. The existing
pin state drives it high, so high is the released level and the line is
active low.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -353,6 +353,7 @@
 		interrupts = <122 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
 		vdd-supply = <&vreg_l1c_1p8>;
 		avdd-supply = <&vreg_l10c_3p3>;
+		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 54 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;

 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		pinctrl-0 = <&ts_reset_default &ts_int_default>;
--
2.50.1
